## Freshservice (ITSM)

Use the freshservice_* tools to read data from a Freshservice (Freshworks) service desk: tickets, problems, changes, releases, assets, requesters, agents, service catalog, knowledge base and more.

* Call `freshservice_list_object_types` first if you are unsure which object_type, include values or sub-resources exist.
* Use `freshservice_search_objects` to find records by field values (server-side filtering). Only some object types are searchable; others must be listed with `freshservice_list_objects` and filtered client-side using the `jq` parameter.
* Use `freshservice_get_object` for full details of one record, and `freshservice_list_related_objects` for a record's conversations, tasks, time_entries or notes.

### IDs

* NEVER guess or fabricate IDs. IDs must come from the user or from a previous tool response.
* Assets and service catalog items are addressed by their `display_id` field, all other objects by `id`.
* Reference fields (requester_id, agent_id, group_id, department_id, ...) contain IDs of other objects; resolve them with `freshservice_get_object` when the user needs names/emails.

### Search query syntax (freshservice_search_objects)

* Conditions: `field:value`, combined with `AND` / `OR`. String values in single quotes, e.g. `status:2 AND priority:4`, `email:'jane@example.com'`, `asset_state:'IN USE'`.
* Date comparisons: `created_at:>'2025-01-01'`, `updated_at:<'2025-06-30'`.
* Tickets/problems/changes use numeric status and priority codes (listed by freshservice_list_object_types). Ticket status: 2=Open, 3=Pending, 4=Resolved, 5=Closed. Priority: 1=Low, 2=Medium, 3=High, 4=Urgent.

### Response size

* Results are paginated (default {{ config.default_page_size if config else 30 }} per page); a `_pagination` entry indicates more pages. Fetch further pages only when needed.
* Ticket descriptions and conversations can be large. Use the `jq` parameter to project only needed fields when listing many records, e.g. `jq='.tickets[] | {id, subject, status, priority}'`.
* An HTTP 403 error means the API key or plan lacks access to that object type - report this instead of retrying.
