### Writing data (create/update/delete)

* `freshservice_create_object` / `freshservice_update_object` / `freshservice_delete_object` modify whole objects; the `*_related_object` variants manage notes, replies, tasks, time entries and custom object records.
* Pass fields as a JSON object string in `object_data`. On update, include ONLY the fields to change.
* Before updating or deleting, fetch the object first to confirm it is the right one. Never guess IDs.
* Creating a ticket requires `subject`, `description`, a requester (`email` or `requester_id`), `status` and `priority` (numeric codes).
* To document investigation findings on a ticket, prefer adding a note (`relation: notes`, body in HTML, `"private": true` unless asked otherwise) over editing the description.
* Deletes are destructive: tickets go to trash, requesters/agents are deactivated. Only delete when the user explicitly asks.
